        "detail": "## Summary\n\n**Task:** Create app/components/index.ts barrel and add ESLint no-restricted-paths rule for components boundary.\n\n**What was done:**\n1. Created `app/components/index.ts` barrel exporting all 8 public components (GameBoard, GameHUD, TileInventory, TilePreview, MobileInventory, WorldGrid, LevelComplete, RainbowArc). Internal utilities (board-utils, canvas-drawing, inventory-shared) are intentionally excluded.\n\n2. Added 2 ESLint `no-restricted-paths` zones in `eslint.config.ts`:\n   - routes → components/!(index).tsx (blocks deep .tsx imports)\n   - routes → components/!(index).ts (blocks deep .ts imports)\n\n3. Updated route files to use barrel imports:\n   - `app/routes/worlds.tsx`: consolidated 2 deep imports into 1 barrel import\n   - `app/routes/play.tsx`: consolidated 5 deep imports into 1 barrel import\n\n4. Updated `zone-boundaries.test.ts`:\n   - Added 2 new expected zone pairs in the config validation test\n   - Added 2 new lint tests: blocks deep component imports from routes, allows barrel imports\n\n**Decisions:**\n- Used both `.tsx` and `.ts` glob patterns in the ESLint rule since the components directory contains both file types\n- Only enforced barrel for routes (the only external consumer), matching the incremental pattern used for hooks barrel enforcement\n- Internal component utilities are not exported through the barrel — they're implementation details\n\n**Results:** All 147 tests pass. Lint clean (1 pre-existing warning)."
